window.DOCS_CONTENT = {
 "title": "Dialogue Component",
 "intro": "Everything you need to build branching, cinematic dialogue in Unreal Engine. The complete guide, hosted right here with every screenshot.",
 "sections": [
  {
   "id": "getting-started",
   "num": "03",
   "icon": "🚀",
   "title": "Getting Started",
   "lede": "Add the component, paste a few nodes, and start authoring branching conversations.",
   "html": "<h3 id=\"getting-started-setup\">Setup</h3><h3 id=\"getting-started-player\">Player</h3><div class=\"doc-step\"><div class=\"doc-step-text\"><p><strong>1.</strong> Open your character blueprint</p><p><strong>2.</strong> Click <strong>(+ Add)</strong>. Add <strong><code>Dialogue_Component</code></strong></p></div><div class=\"doc-step-media\"><img class=\"doc-img\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/docs/gs_step1.png\" data-full=\"assets/docs/gs_step1.png\" alt=\"\" style=\"max-width:400px\"></div></div><div class=\"doc-step\"><div class=\"doc-step-text\"><p><strong>3.</strong> Open <code>BP_DC_TPC</code> (Demo/Blueprints)</p><p><strong>4.</strong> Copy the input node groups into your character</p></div><div class=\"doc-step-media\"><img class=\"doc-img\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/docs/gs_step2.jpg\" data-full=\"assets/docs/gs_step2.jpg\" alt=\"\" style=\"max-width:650px\"></div></div><h3 id=\"getting-started-npc\">NPC</h3><div class=\"doc-step\"><div class=\"doc-step-text\"><p><strong>1.</strong> Add <strong><code>Dialogue_Component</code></strong> to your NPC</p><p><strong>2.</strong> <em>(Optional)</em> Add a <code>Camera</code> component</p></div><div class=\"doc-step-media\"><img class=\"doc-img\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/docs/e133e31c-b07f-413a-9cf8-e8bc7c11a23b.png\" data-full=\"assets/docs/e133e31c-b07f-413a-9cf8-e8bc7c11a23b.png\" alt=\"\"></div></div><p>🎉 <strong>Setup is DONE. Go customize!</strong> 🎉</p><hr><h3 id=\"getting-started-basic-dialogues\">Basic Dialogues</h3><div class=\"doc-step\"><div class=\"doc-step-text\"><p><strong>1.</strong> Select the NPC in your level</p><p>Click <strong>Dialogue_Component</strong> in the Details panel</p></div><div class=\"doc-step-media\"><img class=\"doc-img\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/docs/gs_step3.png\" data-full=\"assets/docs/gs_step3.png\" alt=\"\" style=\"max-width:600px\"></div></div><div class=\"doc-step\"><div class=\"doc-step-text\"><p><strong>2.</strong> Click <strong>(➕)</strong> on <strong>🌿 Dialogue 🌿</strong></p><p>Set <strong>Branch Name</strong> to <code>1</code></p><p><strong>🏁 START 🏁</strong> = <code>1</code> means dialogue opens at branch 1</p><p>No matching Branch Name = no dialogue!</p></div><div class=\"doc-step-media\"><img class=\"doc-img\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/docs/gs_step4.png\" data-full=\"assets/docs/gs_step4.png\" alt=\"\" style=\"max-width:600px\"></div></div><div class=\"doc-step\"><div class=\"doc-step-text\"><p><strong>3.</strong> Type your line into <strong>NPC Text</strong></p><p><strong>Speaker Name</strong> is optional</p></div><div class=\"doc-step-media\"><img class=\"doc-img\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/docs/gs_step5.png\" data-full=\"assets/docs/gs_step5.png\" alt=\"\" style=\"max-width:600px\"></div></div><div class=\"doc-step\"><div class=\"doc-step-text\"><p><strong>4.</strong> Add a choice under <strong>Player</strong> with <strong>(➕)</strong></p><p><strong>Branch Selection</strong> = the branch it leads to</p></div><div class=\"doc-step-media\"><img class=\"doc-img\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/docs/gs_step6.png\" data-full=\"assets/docs/gs_step6.png\" alt=\"\" style=\"max-width:600px\"></div></div><div class=\"doc-step\"><div class=\"doc-step-text\"><p>Blank <strong>Player Text</strong> = green continue button (Zelda style)</p></div><div class=\"doc-step-media\"><img class=\"doc-img\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/docs/1c44c50f-946d-4498-b28c-c80130bc57a5.png\" data-full=\"assets/docs/1c44c50f-946d-4498-b28c-c80130bc57a5.png\" alt=\"\" style=\"max-width:400px\"></div></div><div class=\"doc-step\"><div class=\"doc-step-text\"><p>Any text (even a space) = choice buttons</p></div><div class=\"doc-step-media\"><img class=\"doc-img\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/docs/2c1ad14d-888a-4490-b234-c77b3c22401a.png\" data-full=\"assets/docs/2c1ad14d-888a-4490-b234-c77b3c22401a.png\" alt=\"\" style=\"max-width:400px\"></div></div><div class=\"doc-step\"><div class=\"doc-step-text\"><p><strong>5.</strong> Set <strong>End Dialogue?</strong> = <code>true</code> to close the conversation</p><p>Next interaction reopens at Branch 1</p></div><div class=\"doc-step-media\"><img class=\"doc-img\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/docs/gs_step7.png\" data-full=\"assets/docs/gs_step7.png\" alt=\"\" style=\"max-width:600px\"></div></div><h3 id=\"getting-started-branching-dialogues\">Branching Dialogues</h3><div class=\"doc-step\"><div class=\"doc-step-text\"><p><strong>1.</strong> Point Branch 1's choice at <strong>Branch Selection</strong> = <code>2</code></p><p>Add a branch named <code>2</code> with two choices:</p><p>First choice: continues to Branch 3</p><p>Second choice: ends, resets to Branch 2</p></div><div class=\"doc-step-media\"><img class=\"doc-img\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/docs/c572ceaa-fb52-4f46-9d09-af0504b194f6.png\" data-full=\"assets/docs/c572ceaa-fb52-4f46-9d09-af0504b194f6.png\" alt=\"\" style=\"max-width:400px\"></div></div><div class=\"doc-step\"><div class=\"doc-step-text\"><p><strong>2.</strong> Add branches <code>3</code> and <code>4</code></p><p>Branch 3's choice loops back to Branch 1</p><p>Branch 4 offers an \"End Conversation\" choice</p></div><div class=\"doc-step-media\"><img class=\"doc-img\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/docs/aa7383f2-cae2-43d2-9240-c2d64f4daead.png\" data-full=\"assets/docs/aa7383f2-cae2-43d2-9240-c2d64f4daead.png\" alt=\"\" style=\"max-width:400px\"></div></div><p>Branches connect however you want: loops, dead ends, resets. <strong>Branch Selection</strong> is the wiring</p>"
  },
  {
   "id": "editor",
   "num": "04",
   "icon": "🖥️",
   "title": "Editor Utility Widget",
   "lede": "Keep every variable visible and preview camera angles while you build.",
   "html": "<div class=\"doc-step\"><div class=\"doc-step-text\"><p>The Editor Utility Widget</p><p><strong>\"EUW_DC\"</strong> keeps variables visible at all times, allowing for quick editing & previewing of camera angles</p></div><div class=\"doc-step-media\"><img class=\"doc-img\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/docs/b4a2bf69-1705-440e-a207-60d74b8d499c.png\" data-full=\"assets/docs/b4a2bf69-1705-440e-a207-60d74b8d499c.png\" alt=\"\"></div></div><hr><h3 id=\"editor-how-to-launch\">How To Launch?</h3><div class=\"doc-step\"><div class=\"doc-step-text\"><p>Right-click and run the widget, select an actor, and click <strong>\"Refresh\"</strong></p><p>Notice how the widget will update with the dialogue properties</p><p><</p></div><div class=\"doc-step-media\"><img class=\"doc-img\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/docs/8e50c7d5-0080-4a40-b8b8-2554392ff5bc.gif\" data-full=\"assets/docs/8e50c7d5-0080-4a40-b8b8-2554392ff5bc.gif\" alt=\"GIF 6-5-2025 6-40-48 PM\"></div></div><div class=\"doc-text-block\"><p>></p></div><hr><h3 id=\"editor-how-to-use\">How To Use?</h3><div class=\"doc-step\"><div class=\"doc-step-text\"><p>The editor utility's main function is to help you edit & test changes quickly</p><p>Any changes you make in it will be reflected in the <strong>Details</strong> panel</p></div><div class=\"doc-step-media\"><img class=\"doc-img\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/docs/549f2f04-3f32-4ca8-a737-6d0ebb5d379b.png\" data-full=\"assets/docs/549f2f04-3f32-4ca8-a737-6d0ebb5d379b.png\" alt=\"\"></div></div><div class=\"doc-figure\"><img class=\"doc-img\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/docs/04033f49-fb16-48ac-a82c-86ac9ebd2d8f.gif\" data-full=\"assets/docs/04033f49-fb16-48ac-a82c-86ac9ebd2d8f.gif\" alt=\"GIF 6-5-2025 6-46-42 PM\"></div><hr><h3 id=\"editor-interactive-preview\">Interactive Preview</h3><div class=\"doc-figure\"><img class=\"doc-img\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/docs/euw_panel.jpg\" data-full=\"assets/docs/euw_panel.jpg\" alt=\"\"></div><p>The preview is playable in-editor. Click through dialogue, test choices, even condition-gated ones. No Play needed</p><p>It shows the current branch's camera. Scale the UI with mouse and keyboard</p><h3 id=\"editor-keyboard-shortcuts\">Keyboard Shortcuts</h3><div class=\"doc-text-block\"><p>Shortcut</p><p>Action</p></div><div class=\"doc-text-block\"><p><strong>Ctrl + P</strong></p><p>Toggle the preview window</p></div><div class=\"doc-text-block\"><p><strong>Alt + R</strong></p><p>Refresh the selected actor</p></div><div class=\"doc-text-block\"><p><strong>Arrow Left / Right</strong></p><p>Previous / next branch</p></div><div class=\"doc-text-block\"><p><strong>Arrow keys / D-pad</strong></p><p>Navigate choices in the preview</p></div><p>Refresh also auto-selects the Dialogue Component in Details</p><h3 id=\"editor-other-tools\">Other Tools</h3><ul><li><strong>Function Typer</strong>: run component functions by name</li><li><strong>Collapsible groups</strong>: collapse any variable group</li><li><strong>Data Table import</strong>: the Import button lives here (see Data Tables)</li><li><strong>➕ APPLY ALL</strong>: stamp shared settings onto all branches</li></ul>"
  },
  {
   "id": "global",
   "num": "05",
   "icon": "🛠️",
   "title": "Global Variables",
   "lede": "Apply one set of settings across every branch for simple NPCs.",
   "html": "<h3 id=\"global-global-variables\">Global Variables</h3><p>One settings set for every branch. Great for simple NPCs</p><div class=\"doc-step\"><div class=\"doc-step-text\"><p>Select the NPC's <strong>Dialogue_Component</strong></p><p>Set <strong>⚜ Use Global Variables?</strong> = <code>true</code></p><p>The global structs below it now apply to ALL branches. Per-branch settings are ignored</p></div><div class=\"doc-step-media\"><img class=\"doc-img\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/docs/glob_step1.png\" data-full=\"assets/docs/glob_step1.png\" alt=\"\" style=\"max-width:600px\"></div></div><div class=\"doc-step\"><div class=\"doc-step-text\"><p>The global structs mirror the per-branch ones:</p><p>Auto Complete, Camera, Location, Movement, Rotation, and more</p></div><div class=\"doc-step-media\"><img class=\"doc-img\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/docs/65881bf3-feb0-4186-b73f-4259ba9eaa35.png\" data-full=\"assets/docs/65881bf3-feb0-4186-b73f-4259ba9eaa35.png\" alt=\"\"></div></div>"
  },
  {
   "id": "settings",
   "num": "06",
   "icon": "⚙️",
   "title": "Additional Settings",
   "lede": "Auto-complete, activators, logs, locations, alt buttons, nameplates, visibility, and more.",
   "html": "<h3 id=\"settings-auto-complete\">⚙ Auto Complete</h3><div class=\"doc-step\"><div class=\"doc-step-text\"><p>⚙ <strong>Auto Complete</strong> allows dialogues to progress automatically</p><p>You can disable input/UI for cutscene-style playback, or enable input for timed progression</p></div><div class=\"doc-step-media\"><img class=\"doc-img\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/docs/1d5feca7-1d15-4345-a8d3-262a8790e2df.png\" data-full=\"assets/docs/1d5feca7-1d15-4345-a8d3-262a8790e2df.png\" alt=\"\">\n<img class=\"doc-img\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/docs/c6886632-1fc8-4324-a8a5-232f8cc6efc4.gif\" data-full=\"assets/docs/c6886632-1fc8-4324-a8a5-232f8cc6efc4.gif\" alt=\"\"></div></div><h3 id=\"settings-activator\">🔶 Activator</h3><div class=\"doc-step\"><div class=\"doc-step-text\"><p>In the Showcase level, the 🔶 Activator on Cube 1 triggers Cube 2’s dialogue</p><p>It uses a delay of 0.2s before starting branch 1</p></div><div class=\"doc-step-media\"><img class=\"doc-img\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/docs/a14ad12a-8231-4b24-8454-31faad531527.png\" data-full=\"assets/docs/a14ad12a-8231-4b24-8454-31faad531527.png\" alt=\"\">\n<img class=\"doc-img\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/docs/1b9cb6e8-7554-4d34-9bd5-97605088628d.png\" data-full=\"assets/docs/1b9cb6e8-7554-4d34-9bd5-97605088628d.png\" alt=\"\"></div></div><h3 id=\"settings-destroy\">💥 Destroy</h3><div class=\"doc-step\"><div class=\"doc-step-text\"><p>💥 <strong>Destroy</strong> lets you remove the actor or its interaction ring on a specified branch (e.g., \"Destroy\")</p></div><div class=\"doc-step-media\"><img class=\"doc-img\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/docs/16c94541-489b-4bc4-9e22-5b000ca512c3.png\" data-full=\"assets/docs/16c94541-489b-4bc4-9e22-5b000ca512c3.png\" alt=\"\"></div></div><h3 id=\"settings-logs\">💬 Logs</h3><div class=\"doc-step\"><div class=\"doc-step-text\"><p>Dialogue logs show past NPC and player responses</p></div><div class=\"doc-step-media\"><img class=\"doc-img\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/docs/e83bc512-dc55-42aa-8104-9633d88f8ff0.png\" data-full=\"assets/docs/e83bc512-dc55-42aa-8104-9633d88f8ff0.png\" alt=\"\">\n<img class=\"doc-img\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/docs/af6eacf9-6195-417f-846d-312f024f2f5a.png\" data-full=\"assets/docs/af6eacf9-6195-417f-846d-312f024f2f5a.png\" alt=\"\">\n<img class=\"doc-img\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/docs/4defd179-4ae6-4391-9964-b4bc324e656f.png\" data-full=\"assets/docs/4defd179-4ae6-4391-9964-b4bc324e656f.png\" alt=\"\">\n<img class=\"doc-img\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/docs/52dde1de-fadf-4707-b54f-760a71f1c062.png\" data-full=\"assets/docs/52dde1de-fadf-4707-b54f-760a71f1c062.png\" alt=\"\"></div></div><h3 id=\"settings-location\">🌍 Location</h3><div class=\"doc-step\"><div class=\"doc-step-text\"><p>Two types of location settings: player teleport and NPC movement</p><p>If <strong>Player Move To Location</strong> is true and a <code>BP_PlayerLocation</code> is present, player teleports to it during dialogue</p></div><div class=\"doc-step-media\"><img class=\"doc-img\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/docs/261b4b68-b54b-4018-b1a0-307800092787.png\" data-full=\"assets/docs/261b4b68-b54b-4018-b1a0-307800092787.png\" alt=\"\">\n<img class=\"doc-img\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/docs/412c3f65-e6f3-4fc6-8c15-96a0522a2333.png\" data-full=\"assets/docs/412c3f65-e6f3-4fc6-8c15-96a0522a2333.png\" alt=\"\"></div></div><div class=\"doc-step\"><div class=\"doc-step-text\"><p>NPCs can also move to locations on interaction</p></div><div class=\"doc-step-media\"><img class=\"doc-img\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/docs/5f0b0678-f5c0-48d4-a8bb-ba605b923c3f.png\" data-full=\"assets/docs/5f0b0678-f5c0-48d4-a8bb-ba605b923c3f.png\" alt=\"\"></div></div><div class=\"doc-step\"><div class=\"doc-step-text\"><p>If <strong>Use Global</strong> is true, movement occurs on all interactions. If false, movement happens only on specified branches</p></div><div class=\"doc-step-media\"><img class=\"doc-img\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/docs/b5de7e0b-73d0-4712-99cc-762263e20916.png\" data-full=\"assets/docs/b5de7e0b-73d0-4712-99cc-762263e20916.png\" alt=\"\"></div></div><div class=\"doc-step\"><div class=\"doc-step-text\"><p>You can also attach <code>BP_PlayerLocation</code> to your character to preview where the player will appear</p></div><div class=\"doc-step-media\"><img class=\"doc-img\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/docs/12012d47-8a85-43f8-8538-c61a1d9f615a.png\" data-full=\"assets/docs/12012d47-8a85-43f8-8538-c61a1d9f615a.png\" alt=\"\"></div></div><div class=\"doc-step\"><div class=\"doc-step-text\"><p>Press <strong>Refresh</strong> to generate a preview mesh that displays the player’s set location and rotation in-game</p></div><div class=\"doc-step-media\"><img class=\"doc-img\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/docs/c4703e7d-b4b0-4ddc-a4e9-90aadb25d785.png\" data-full=\"assets/docs/c4703e7d-b4b0-4ddc-a4e9-90aadb25d785.png\" alt=\"\"></div></div><h3 id=\"settings-animations-audio\">🤺 Animations & 🔊 Audio</h3><div class=\"doc-step\"><div class=\"doc-step-text\"><p>Animations and sounds can be added through ➕ Extra Settings</p><p>You can add multiple entries—arrays support multi-action playback</p></div><div class=\"doc-step-media\"><img class=\"doc-img\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/docs/28fe1863-70ac-4785-977c-de8f389f4b4d.png\" data-full=\"assets/docs/28fe1863-70ac-4785-977c-de8f389f4b4d.png\" alt=\"\"></div></div><div class=\"doc-step\"><div class=\"doc-step-text\"><p>These settings are also editable in the Editor Utility</p></div><div class=\"doc-step-media\"><img class=\"doc-img\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/docs/9e75ff87-479f-4cae-9b3a-b248176a6bd8.gif\" data-full=\"assets/docs/9e75ff87-479f-4cae-9b3a-b248176a6bd8.gif\" alt=\"\"></div></div><h3 id=\"settings-alternative-buttons\">🎮 Alternative Buttons</h3><div class=\"doc-step\"><div class=\"doc-step-text\"><p>An alternative input system is available for dialogue choices, inspired by games like <em>Telltale</em>, <em>Detroit: Become Human</em>, and <em>Oxenfree</em></p><p>Instead of one button for all choices, this system allows separate inputs per option</p></div><div class=\"doc-step-media\"><img class=\"doc-img\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/docs/pie_alt_buttons.jpg\" data-full=\"assets/docs/pie_alt_buttons.jpg\" alt=\"\" style=\"max-width:700px\">\n<img class=\"doc-img\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/docs/94e74d98-54e5-47ea-a697-1631be3ff576.png\" data-full=\"assets/docs/94e74d98-54e5-47ea-a697-1631be3ff576.png\" alt=\"\"></div></div><div class=\"doc-step\"><div class=\"doc-step-text\"><p>To use it, enable <strong>Use Buttons?</strong> in the settings</p><p>Default keys are 1–4 on keyboard and A/B/X/Y on Xbox controller</p><p>If used with Auto Complete, the system will randomly choose an available option when the timer ends</p></div><div class=\"doc-step-media\"><img class=\"doc-img\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/docs/7b5b2ba6-21fd-4df4-bc2b-a313a0e57533.png\" data-full=\"assets/docs/7b5b2ba6-21fd-4df4-bc2b-a313a0e57533.png\" alt=\"\"></div></div><div class=\"doc-step\"><div class=\"doc-step-text\"><p>Button layouts, input bindings, and visual styles can be customized in the <strong>🎮 Alt Button</strong> struct</p><p>The NPC using this system must include the <code>W_Alt_Buttons</code> widget and its logic</p><p>A complete setup is already implemented in a sample NPC. Duplicate or create a child for your own use</p></div><div class=\"doc-step-media\"><img class=\"doc-img\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/docs/580e3f1f-fd8f-482a-84cf-30928c5341ff.png\" data-full=\"assets/docs/580e3f1f-fd8f-482a-84cf-30928c5341ff.png\" alt=\"\"></div></div><h3 id=\"settings-nameplate-ui\">🏷️ Nameplate UI</h3><div class=\"doc-figure\"><img class=\"doc-img\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/docs/feace594-20db-4e73-8808-4beba52de021.png\" data-full=\"assets/docs/feace594-20db-4e73-8808-4beba52de021.png\" alt=\"\"></div><div class=\"doc-step\"><div class=\"doc-step-text\"><p>When the bool is set to true, the below settings are applied to the current branch</p></div><div class=\"doc-step-media\"><img class=\"doc-img\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/docs/pie_nameplate.jpg\" data-full=\"assets/docs/pie_nameplate.jpg\" alt=\"\" style=\"max-width:700px\"></div></div><div class=\"doc-step\"><div class=\"doc-step-text\"><p>The example below first starts with the NPC preset, shows both sprites, and focuses on the right sprite</p><p>The next branch uses the Player preset, both sprites, and uses the left sprite</p><p>_<strong>⚠️ The preview window may not perfectly reflect what is shown in gameplay ⚠️</strong>_</p></div><div class=\"doc-step-media\"><img class=\"doc-img\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/docs/5f93954f-9f12-456a-9785-6a3a5ed3b160.gif\" data-full=\"assets/docs/5f93954f-9f12-456a-9785-6a3a5ed3b160.gif\" alt=\"\"></div></div><div class=\"doc-step\"><div class=\"doc-step-text\"><p>You can edit the preset properties under the preset struct within the component</p><p>After setting the properties in the preset window, just put the name of the preset to use in the editor utility and it will be selected</p><p>_<strong>To darken a sprite, simply adjust the tint so that it's darker.</strong>_</p></div><div class=\"doc-step-media\"><img class=\"doc-img\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/docs/7ba1cdad-fc94-43f8-a621-97c775549cd5.png\" data-full=\"assets/docs/7ba1cdad-fc94-43f8-a621-97c775549cd5.png\" alt=\"\"></div></div><h3 id=\"settings-visibility\">👁️ Visibility</h3><div class=\"doc-step\"><div class=\"doc-step-text\"><p>You can change the visibility of the player and the actor they’re talking to by enabling the appropriate settings in the <strong>Dialogue Component</strong></p></div><div class=\"doc-step-media\"><img class=\"doc-img\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/docs/999465ce-f166-4fbb-ac2b-2b746af0373e.png\" data-full=\"assets/docs/999465ce-f166-4fbb-ac2b-2b746af0373e.png\" alt=\"\" style=\"max-width:400px\"></div></div><div class=\"doc-step\"><div class=\"doc-step-text\"><p>For modular characters composed of multiple body parts (children), set <strong>Propagate to Children</strong> to <code>true</code> to ensure visibility is applied consistently</p></div><div class=\"doc-step-media\"><img class=\"doc-img\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/docs/1381f09e-a21e-4d2c-8eef-3644e57cad61.png\" data-full=\"assets/docs/1381f09e-a21e-4d2c-8eef-3644e57cad61.png\" alt=\"\" style=\"max-width:400px\"></div></div><div class=\"doc-step\"><div class=\"doc-step-text\"><p>⚠️ Attached objects (like weapons, scrolls, or accessories) may inherit visibility settings unexpectedly</p><p>In this example, the player has a scroll and an icon attached</p></div><div class=\"doc-step-media\"><img class=\"doc-img\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/docs/1eefbe3f-c1bc-45ec-9a1f-e3fbfe0dcc95.png\" data-full=\"assets/docs/1eefbe3f-c1bc-45ec-9a1f-e3fbfe0dcc95.png\" alt=\"\" style=\"max-width:400px\"></div></div><div class=\"doc-step\"><div class=\"doc-step-text\"><p>When dialogue begins, everything disappears as expected. But when it ends, unintended elements (like the logo) may reappear</p></div><div class=\"doc-step-media\"><img class=\"doc-img\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/docs/83528d39-38e5-406a-8c8f-b50621791b5e.gif\" data-full=\"assets/docs/83528d39-38e5-406a-8c8f-b50621791b5e.gif\" alt=\"\"></div></div><div class=\"doc-step\"><div class=\"doc-step-text\"><p>To prevent this, add specific tags to the <strong>Visibility Tags</strong> array. Only components with those tags will be affected</p></div><div class=\"doc-step-media\"><img class=\"doc-img\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/docs/f5c5e19e-6dda-4c8f-b61f-44f213041497.png\" data-full=\"assets/docs/f5c5e19e-6dda-4c8f-b61f-44f213041497.png\" alt=\"\"></div></div><div class=\"doc-step\"><div class=\"doc-step-text\"><p>In this case, we added the tag <strong>\"Visibility\"</strong> to both the player and the NPC</p></div><div class=\"doc-step-media\"><img class=\"doc-img\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/docs/94a691cb-65ac-40f9-9b50-1aaef1027c9c.png\" data-full=\"assets/docs/94a691cb-65ac-40f9-9b50-1aaef1027c9c.png\" alt=\"\"></div></div><div class=\"doc-step\"><div class=\"doc-step-text\"><p>✅ Now, when the dialogue ends, the scroll and icon no longer reappear</p></div><div class=\"doc-step-media\"><img class=\"doc-img\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/docs/311cd1a9-3dfc-4a27-8b9f-b7e3801ba0be.gif\" data-full=\"assets/docs/311cd1a9-3dfc-4a27-8b9f-b7e3801ba0be.gif\" alt=\"\"></div></div><h3 id=\"settings-auto-start\">⚙ Auto Start</h3><div class=\"doc-text-block\"><p>Start dialogue without the interact key:</p><p><strong>Begin Play?</strong>: starts when the level starts</p><p><strong>Overlap (Self)?</strong>: starts on entering interaction range</p><p><strong>Overlap (Other)?</strong>: starts on overlapping listed actors (triggers, doorways)</p><p>Related:</p><p><strong>⚙ Talk Once?</strong>: one conversation only (saved)</p><p><strong>Disable Input Until Overlap Again?</strong>: re-enter range to talk again</p><p><strong>Start From Overlap End?</strong>: trigger on leaving instead</p></div><h3 id=\"settings-name-replacement\">🗣 Name Replacement</h3><div class=\"doc-text-block\"><p>Auto-populates speaker names inside dialogue text</p><p><strong>Name Search NPC / Player</strong>: placeholder text replaced with the real name. Write once, every NPC says the right name</p><p><strong>Prefix / Suffix</strong>, <strong>Decision Prefix / Suffix</strong>: auto-wrapped around names and choices. Style once, not per line</p></div><h3 id=\"settings-level-sequences\">🎬 Level Sequences</h3><div class=\"doc-text-block\"><p>Play a <strong>Level Sequence</strong> per branch (➕ Extra Settings). Cutscenes inside conversations</p><p><strong>🎬 Level Sequence</strong>: the sequence to play</p><p><strong>🎬 Level Sequence Settings</strong>: playback options (loop, rate, hide player...)</p><p>Example: <code>Examples/Saving/Cutscene</code></p></div><h3 id=\"settings-money-ui\">💰 Money UI</h3><div class=\"doc-text-block\"><p>Currency display for shop NPCs (like the demo's gold)</p><p><strong>💰 Show UI?</strong>: show the money widget</p><p><strong>💰 Fade In / Out?</strong>: fade instead of pop</p><p><strong>💰 Decorator</strong>: rich text style for the amount</p></div><h3 id=\"settings-skip-branch\">⏩ Skip Branch</h3><div class=\"doc-step\"><div class=\"doc-step-text\"><p>The <strong>\"E\" key</strong> is used for dialogue interactions</p><p>A bool can register a regular input as a skip</p></div><div class=\"doc-step-media\"><img class=\"doc-img\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/docs/2954845a-59b5-4a53-a672-b6ae4f5b88f1.png\" data-full=\"assets/docs/2954845a-59b5-4a53-a672-b6ae4f5b88f1.png\" alt=\"\"></div></div><div class=\"doc-step\"><div class=\"doc-step-text\"><p>A new field under 🎭 <strong>Player Choices</strong> lets you specify a branch for the skip button</p></div><div class=\"doc-step-media\"><img class=\"doc-img\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/docs/94eec95a-ad0b-4e0f-8592-a4714ca67fe0.png\" data-full=\"assets/docs/94eec95a-ad0b-4e0f-8592-a4714ca67fe0.png\" alt=\"\"></div></div><div class=\"doc-step\"><div class=\"doc-step-text\"><p>Setting <strong>Skip To Branch</strong> to <code>3</code> makes the player get thanked for a purchase (even if none was made)</p><p>Adding <code>[end]</code> immediately after the branch (no spaces) ends dialogue and resumes at the specified branch</p></div><div class=\"doc-step-media\"><img class=\"doc-img\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/docs/194c4f8e-d597-48fc-93d6-87dc822b7c30.gif\" data-full=\"assets/docs/194c4f8e-d597-48fc-93d6-87dc822b7c30.gif\" alt=\"\"></div></div><div class=\"doc-step\"><div class=\"doc-step-text\"><p>If left blank, the skip input will default to the regular branch tied to the player's selected choice</p><p>You can also delete the skip input from the widget if you don’t want it available</p></div><div class=\"doc-step-media\"><img class=\"doc-img\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/docs/ad036f0a-4ab2-45c2-9cd2-efc4fd088274.png\" data-full=\"assets/docs/ad036f0a-4ab2-45c2-9cd2-efc4fd088274.png\" alt=\"\"></div></div>"
  },
  {
   "id": "conditions",
   "num": "07",
   "icon": "⚖️",
   "title": "Conditions",
   "lede": "Gate responses on player stats with pass / fail states.",
   "html": "<h3 id=\"conditions-conditions\">Conditions</h3><p>Gate choices behind requirements: gold, items, evidence, anything countable</p><p>Conditions live on the <strong>player's</strong> Dialogue Component. Each is a name + number</p><div class=\"doc-figure\"><img class=\"doc-img\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/docs/pie_shop_choices.jpg\" data-full=\"assets/docs/pie_shop_choices.jpg\" alt=\"\" style=\"max-width:700px\"></div><h3 id=\"conditions-where-they-live\">Where They Live</h3><div class=\"doc-step\"><div class=\"doc-step-text\"><p>Every player choice has a <strong>📝 Player Conditions</strong> struct</p><p>It gates that one choice</p></div><div class=\"doc-step-media\"><img class=\"doc-img\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/docs/cond_step1.png\" data-full=\"assets/docs/cond_step1.png\" alt=\"\" style=\"max-width:600px\"></div></div><div class=\"doc-step\"><div class=\"doc-step-text\"><p>The struct, field by field:</p><p><strong>Condition</strong>: the requirement map (name + amount needed)</p><p><strong>Change Branch?</strong>: <code>true</code> enables pass/fail routing. Required for gates!</p><p><strong>Condition Type</strong>: Subtract, Add, or Nothing on evaluation</p><p><strong>✔ PASSED / ✔ Pass Condition</strong>: branch + deltas on success</p><p><strong>❌ FAILED / ❌ Fail Condition</strong>: branch + deltas on failure</p><p><strong>❌ Button Fail State</strong>: Nothing, Deactivate (gray), or Hide</p></div><div class=\"doc-step-media\"><img class=\"doc-img\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/docs/cond_step2.png\" data-full=\"assets/docs/cond_step2.png\" alt=\"\" style=\"max-width:600px\"></div></div><p>⚠ A gated choice routes ONLY via ✔/❌ branches. Leave its <strong>Branch Selection</strong> empty; that jump ignores the condition</p><h3 id=\"conditions-examples\">Examples</h3><div class=\"doc-text-block\"><p>Example</p><p>Image</p></div><div class=\"doc-step\"><div class=\"doc-step-text\"><p><strong>DC_Demo shop</strong>: beer costs 3 gold</p><p>Checks <strong>Gold ≥ 3</strong>. Pass: subtract, go Branch 3. Fail: Branch 4</p></div><div class=\"doc-step-media\"><img class=\"doc-img\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/docs/e6df9909-884f-448d-a6c1-ea8180361a45.png\" data-full=\"assets/docs/e6df9909-884f-448d-a6c1-ea8180361a45.png\" alt=\"\"></div></div><div class=\"doc-step\"><div class=\"doc-step-text\"><p><strong>DC_Interrogation</strong>: needs <strong>Evidence ≥ 1</strong></p><p>Fail State = <strong>Deactivate</strong>: the choice grays out</p></div><div class=\"doc-step-media\"><img class=\"doc-img\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/docs/c02c30ae-baeb-4f9c-9fa5-2228392744b6.png\" data-full=\"assets/docs/c02c30ae-baeb-4f9c-9fa5-2228392744b6.png\" alt=\"\"></div></div><div class=\"doc-step\"><div class=\"doc-step-text\"><p>Fail State = <strong>Hide</strong>: the choice disappears</p></div><div class=\"doc-step-media\"><img class=\"doc-img\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/docs/a9106500-a846-47a3-9af8-57f93ad27eb9.png\" data-full=\"assets/docs/a9106500-a846-47a3-9af8-57f93ad27eb9.png\" alt=\"\"></div></div><h3 id=\"conditions-granting-conditions\">Granting Conditions</h3><p>Call <strong>Change Player Condition Single</strong> from any blueprint (pickup, quest, kill). See Events & Blueprint Nodes</p>"
  },
  {
   "id": "rich-text",
   "num": "08",
   "icon": "🎨",
   "title": "Rich Text, Icons & Fonts",
   "lede": "Style text inline with color tags, icons, and custom fonts.",
   "html": "<h3 id=\"rich-text-rich-text-icons\">🎨 Rich Text & Icons</h3><div class=\"doc-figure\"><img class=\"doc-img\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/docs/819cdf26-6efb-456a-ba31-e993f301fad7.png\" data-full=\"assets/docs/819cdf26-6efb-456a-ba31-e993f301fad7.png\" alt=\"\"></div><p><br> These data tables hold the tags for stylized fonts and icons <br><br> <p align=\"center\"></p> <br><br> <p align=\"center\"></p> <br><br> Usage examples: <br><br> <p align=\"center\"></p> <br><br> <p align=\"center\"></p> <br><br> <strong>Tag Format:</strong> DB = Default Blue DG = Default Green IR = Italics Red BY = Bold Yellow <br><br> <strong>Icon Format:</strong> Talk1 = <img class=\"inline-icon\" src=\"assets/docs/da3aa086-3738-4632-ac5b-b0daebf223d0.png\" data-full=\"assets/docs/da3aa086-3738-4632-ac5b-b0daebf223d0.png\" alt=\"\"> Talk2 = <img class=\"inline-icon\" src=\"assets/docs/769ba7f1-0f29-4a78-8df9-cd2cc450f988.png\" data-full=\"assets/docs/769ba7f1-0f29-4a78-8df9-cd2cc450f988.png\" alt=\"\"> Map__ = <img class=\"inline-icon\" src=\"assets/docs/4d24c934-a265-4c47-868a-7daf6a7e1c9f.png\" data-full=\"assets/docs/4d24c934-a265-4c47-868a-7daf6a7e1c9f.png\" alt=\"\"> |</p><div class=\"doc-figure\"><img class=\"doc-img\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/docs/a298e7a3-4cbb-4356-a0e3-3de3d7b0753f.png\" data-full=\"assets/docs/a298e7a3-4cbb-4356-a0e3-3de3d7b0753f.png\" alt=\"\"><img class=\"doc-img\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/docs/fcfe3e38-26b1-4d31-9330-ba54b0ccaa80.png\" data-full=\"assets/docs/fcfe3e38-26b1-4d31-9330-ba54b0ccaa80.png\" alt=\"\"><img class=\"doc-img\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/docs/3136b4c7-c1a3-4545-aea8-0785a2d9faa9.png\" data-full=\"assets/docs/3136b4c7-c1a3-4545-aea8-0785a2d9faa9.png\" alt=\"\"><img class=\"doc-img\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/docs/82240f17-0f1c-44eb-9753-a4d0a21a10cc.png\" data-full=\"assets/docs/82240f17-0f1c-44eb-9753-a4d0a21a10cc.png\" alt=\"\"></div><hr><h3 id=\"rich-text-font-settings\">🅰️ Font Settings</h3><div class=\"doc-figure\"><img class=\"doc-img\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/docs/c20317d6-412b-4bd0-b98c-76003df20c4a.png\" data-full=\"assets/docs/c20317d6-412b-4bd0-b98c-76003df20c4a.png\" alt=\"\"></div><p><br> Open this asset. Assign your custom fonts <br><br> <p align=\"center\"></p> <br><br> ⚠️ Changes may need a project restart <br><br> 🔠 Font Size <br> No in-editor solution yet. Manage sizes via a linked spreadsheet <br><br> <p align=\"center\"></p> |</p><div class=\"doc-figure\"><img class=\"doc-img\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/docs/6d020a64-0b2a-4523-a32f-117fc3a2a565.png\" data-full=\"assets/docs/6d020a64-0b2a-4523-a32f-117fc3a2a565.png\" alt=\"\"><img class=\"doc-img\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/docs/49a5cc10-f563-468b-b42a-5b89c75ac286.png\" data-full=\"assets/docs/49a5cc10-f563-468b-b42a-5b89c75ac286.png\" alt=\"\"></div>"
  },
  {
   "id": "ui",
   "num": "09",
   "icon": "🎛️",
   "title": "UI Customization",
   "lede": "Two ways to restyle the dialogue UI, with live preview.",
   "html": "<h3 id=\"ui-ui-customization\">UI Customization</h3><p>Two ways to style the UI</p><h3 id=\"ui-1-ui-presets-recommended\">1. UI Presets (recommended)</h3><div class=\"doc-step\"><div class=\"doc-step-text\"><p>Select the <strong>Dialogue_Component</strong>. Open <strong>🎨 UI Presets</strong></p><p><strong>Style To Use</strong>: the active preset's name</p><p><strong>Styles</strong>: the preset map. Add your own</p></div><div class=\"doc-step-media\"><img class=\"doc-img\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/docs/ui_step1.png\" data-full=\"assets/docs/ui_step1.png\" alt=\"\" style=\"max-width:600px\"></div></div><div class=\"doc-step\"><div class=\"doc-step-text\"><p>Preview and adjust live in the Editor Utility</p></div><div class=\"doc-step-media\"><img class=\"doc-img\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/docs/4521bdf8-076b-4cf0-86ce-055571d0d79e.gif\" data-full=\"assets/docs/4521bdf8-076b-4cf0-86ce-055571d0d79e.gif\" alt=\"\"></div></div><div class=\"doc-step\"><div class=\"doc-step-text\"><p>Changes show instantly</p></div><div class=\"doc-step-media\"><img class=\"doc-img\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/docs/9588b33b-b8b1-4818-a2e9-2f623882dd92.gif\" data-full=\"assets/docs/9588b33b-b8b1-4818-a2e9-2f623882dd92.gif\" alt=\"\"></div></div><h3 id=\"ui-2-edit-the-widgets-directly\">2. Edit the widgets directly</h3><div class=\"doc-step\"><div class=\"doc-step-text\"><p>Editing <code>W_Dialogue</code> yourself? Set <strong>🎨 Use UI Struct?</strong> = <code>false</code></p><p>The component stops overriding your widget edits</p></div><div class=\"doc-step-media\"><img class=\"doc-img\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/docs/fe7b5816-7802-4c04-8501-c5735e9c2b66.png\" data-full=\"assets/docs/fe7b5816-7802-4c04-8501-c5735e9c2b66.png\" alt=\"\"></div></div>"
  },
  {
   "id": "save",
   "num": "10",
   "icon": "💾",
   "title": "Save System",
   "lede": "Persist actor transforms, branches, and conditions, then restore them on load.",
   "html": "<h3 id=\"save-save-system\">Save System</h3><p>Saves actor transforms, START branches, conditions, destroyed actors, and Talk Once state</p><p><code>BP_DC_Save</code> (the DC Save REF) holds it all in one struct</p><h3 id=\"save-enable-it\">Enable It</h3><div class=\"doc-step\"><div class=\"doc-step-text\"><p>On the <strong>Player's</strong> Dialogue Component, open <strong>💾 Save Settings</strong></p><p><strong>Slot Name</strong>: the save file's name</p><p><strong>Use Save?</strong> = <code>true</code> enables the built-in save</p><p><strong>Load Player / Actor Transforms?</strong>: what gets restored</p><p><code>Use Save?</code> off? The struct still updates. Feed it to your own save system</p></div><div class=\"doc-step-media\"><img class=\"doc-img\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/docs/save_step1.png\" data-full=\"assets/docs/save_step1.png\" alt=\"\" style=\"max-width:600px\"></div></div><h3 id=\"save-how-it-works\">How It Works</h3><div class=\"doc-step\"><div class=\"doc-step-text\"><p><code>BP_DC_TPC</code> ships save/load key events. Copy or call them</p></div><div class=\"doc-step-media\"><img class=\"doc-img\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/docs/c03afbdc-f3b9-45f2-96bc-eba104b138da.png\" data-full=\"assets/docs/c03afbdc-f3b9-45f2-96bc-eba104b138da.png\" alt=\"image\"></div></div><div class=\"doc-step\"><div class=\"doc-step-text\"><p><strong>Save Game</strong>: creates the slot if missing</p><p>Loops all DC actors. Stores transforms, START branches, player conditions</p></div><div class=\"doc-step-media\"><img class=\"doc-img\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/docs/346249a8-d08e-4fd5-acf1-43cee14fe739.png\" data-full=\"assets/docs/346249a8-d08e-4fd5-acf1-43cee14fe739.png\" alt=\"image\"></div></div><div class=\"doc-step\"><div class=\"doc-step-text\"><p><strong>Load</strong>: reads the struct back</p><p>Restores each actor's transform and START branch</p></div><div class=\"doc-step-media\"><img class=\"doc-img\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/docs/b5041f37-c496-491f-9042-fa3c3da06f5e.png\" data-full=\"assets/docs/b5041f37-c496-491f-9042-fa3c3da06f5e.png\" alt=\"image\"></div></div><h3 id=\"save-with-other-save-systems\">With Other Save Systems</h3><p>Call the DC's save/load logic from your asset's save button. Full or partial; your choice. <strong>Get DC Player's Save REF</strong> exposes the struct</p>"
  },
  {
   "id": "moving-actor",
   "num": "11",
   "icon": "🎬",
   "title": "Moving Actor & Camera Tracker",
   "lede": "Spline-driven cinematic rails and consistent camera framing.",
   "html": "<h3 id=\"moving-actor-moving-actor-camera-tracker\">Moving Actor & Camera Tracker</h3><div class=\"doc-text-block\"><p>🎬 BP_MovingActor</p></div><div class=\"doc-step\"><div class=\"doc-step-text\"><p>Multifunction actor: camera control and spline movement</p><p>Supports <strong>Look At</strong> targets, fades, and focus settings</p></div><div class=\"doc-step-media\"><img class=\"doc-img\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/docs/95156fc1-2747-46fd-ab8a-9a0122ca78b7.png\" data-full=\"assets/docs/95156fc1-2747-46fd-ab8a-9a0122ca78b7.png\" alt=\"\"></div></div><div class=\"doc-step\"><div class=\"doc-step-text\"><p>Moves along splines: cinematic rail, platform, door, elevator</p></div><div class=\"doc-step-media\"><img class=\"doc-img\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/docs/5545a3cd-d9e6-4999-9b92-d1a6437455b7.png\" data-full=\"assets/docs/5545a3cd-d9e6-4999-9b92-d1a6437455b7.png\" alt=\"\"></div></div><div class=\"doc-step\"><div class=\"doc-step-text\"><p>Can trigger a branch change when the spline finishes</p></div><div class=\"doc-step-media\"><img class=\"doc-img\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/docs/a9e80284-3515-4a1e-8450-b6b72bae7ade.png\" data-full=\"assets/docs/a9e80284-3515-4a1e-8450-b6b72bae7ade.png\" alt=\"\"></div></div><div class=\"doc-text-block\"><p>A 🎯 Target Actor can ride the spline. See the Showcase helicopter</p></div><div class=\"doc-text-block\"><p>🎥 BP_CameraTracker</p></div><div class=\"doc-step\"><div class=\"doc-step-text\"><p>Works like <code>BP_PlayerLocation</code>. Attach it to your actor</p><p>Cameras track this point during <code>BP_MovingActor</code> moves</p><p>Fixes inconsistent LookAt offsets between characters</p></div><div class=\"doc-step-media\"><img class=\"doc-img\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/docs/b453cd40-7a7e-4a4d-8a3c-af4583710b28.png\" data-full=\"assets/docs/b453cd40-7a7e-4a4d-8a3c-af4583710b28.png\" alt=\"\"></div></div>"
  },
  {
   "id": "data-tables",
   "num": "12",
   "icon": "📊",
   "title": "Data Tables",
   "lede": "Author whole conversations in a spreadsheet and import them by name.",
   "html": "<h3 id=\"data-tables-data-tables\">Data Tables</h3><p>Write dialogue in a spreadsheet. Import it as branches</p><p>Sample CSV <a href=\"https://mega.nz/file/NbMlkAKY#eqJEnkJHq2ZPZgz6hJZQrt3DJ_yg_Yqw7KzslqJmsL0\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">here</a></p><h3 id=\"data-tables-setup\">Setup</h3><div class=\"doc-step\"><div class=\"doc-step-text\"><p><strong>1.</strong> Select the Dialogue_Component. Search \"data table\"</p><p>Assign your <strong>Data Table</strong> asset</p></div><div class=\"doc-step-media\"><img class=\"doc-img\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/docs/dt_step1.png\" data-full=\"assets/docs/dt_step1.png\" alt=\"\" style=\"max-width:600px\"></div></div><div class=\"doc-step\"><div class=\"doc-step-text\"><p><strong>2.</strong> Open <strong>DT_Dialogue</strong> to see a sample</p><p>Link it to a CSV for easy updating</p></div><div class=\"doc-step-media\"><img class=\"doc-img\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/docs/ce809d2c-aca9-4fa0-a76c-77684f0cb0c8.png\" data-full=\"assets/docs/ce809d2c-aca9-4fa0-a76c-77684f0cb0c8.png\" alt=\"\"></div></div><div class=\"doc-step\"><div class=\"doc-step-text\"><p><strong>3.</strong> Press <strong>Import</strong> in the Editor Utility</p><p>With a file path: updates the table AND builds branches</p><p>Without: builds branches from the existing table</p></div><div class=\"doc-step-media\"><img class=\"doc-img\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/docs/363954d1-031e-4e3d-b26a-9024546ee501.png\" data-full=\"assets/docs/363954d1-031e-4e3d-b26a-9024546ee501.png\" alt=\"\"></div></div><div class=\"doc-step\"><div class=\"doc-step-text\"><p>Export anytime: right-click the table → <strong>Export</strong> → edit in Excel</p></div><div class=\"doc-step-media\"><img class=\"doc-img\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/docs/8a0c7357-612d-4811-bb68-9c376fccfca2.png\" data-full=\"assets/docs/8a0c7357-612d-4811-bb68-9c376fccfca2.png\" alt=\"\"></div></div><h3 id=\"data-tables-csv-rules\">CSV Rules</h3><p>🟩 Only rows with <strong>START</strong> filled become branches 🟧 Choices: copy the START value, name the Speaker <code>Choice1</code>, <code>Choice2</code>... 🟪 Booleans: type <code>t</code> for true 🟨 Audio/animations: asset name only. The system finds it</p><div class=\"doc-figure\"><img class=\"doc-img\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/docs/c5a0fb37-acd7-4877-a9d2-854fbbd75b62.png\" data-full=\"assets/docs/c5a0fb37-acd7-4877-a9d2-854fbbd75b62.png\" alt=\"\"></div><p>Empty rows are skipped. Space things out freely</p><p>Conditions format: <code>((\"Energy\", 1),(\"Money\", 5))</code></p><p>Unsure about a format? Edit the table in Unreal, export, and copy what it wrote</p>"
  },
  {
   "id": "cameras",
   "num": "13",
   "icon": "🎥",
   "title": "Cameras",
   "lede": "Per-branch camera switching, presets, shakes, and blends.",
   "html": "<h3 id=\"cameras-cameras\">Cameras</h3><p>Per-branch camera switching, reusable presets, shakes, and blends</p><div class=\"doc-figure\"><img class=\"doc-img\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/docs/pie_camera.jpg\" data-full=\"assets/docs/pie_camera.jpg\" alt=\"\" style=\"max-width:700px\"></div><h3 id=\"cameras-camera-sources\">Camera Sources</h3><div class=\"doc-text-block\"><p>Type</p><p>How it works</p></div><div class=\"doc-text-block\"><p><strong>NPC Attached Camera</strong></p><p>Add a <code>Camera</code> component to your NPC. Enable <strong>Use NPC Camera?</strong></p></div><div class=\"doc-text-block\"><p><strong>Cine Camera</strong></p><p>Attached <code>CineCamera</code> components work too</p></div><div class=\"doc-text-block\"><p><strong>Camera Presets</strong></p><p>Place <code>BP_CC_NPC</code>, <code>BP_CC_Player</code>, or <code>BP_CC_Environment</code> in your level. Point any branch at them</p></div><div class=\"doc-text-block\"><p><strong>Specific Camera</strong></p><p>Reference any level camera directly, per branch</p></div><h3 id=\"cameras-per-branch-camera-settings\">Per-Branch Camera Settings</h3><p>Each branch has a <strong>🎥 Camera</strong> struct:</p><div class=\"doc-figure\"><img class=\"doc-img\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/docs/euw_camera_settings.jpg\" data-full=\"assets/docs/euw_camera_settings.jpg\" alt=\"\" style=\"max-width:400px\"></div><div class=\"doc-text-block\"><p>Property</p><p>Description</p></div><div class=\"doc-text-block\"><p><strong>Use Camera?</strong></p><p>Enables the camera change this branch</p></div><div class=\"doc-text-block\"><p><strong>Preset</strong></p><p>Which camera type/preset to use</p></div><div class=\"doc-text-block\"><p><strong>Switch Delay</strong></p><p>Wait before switching</p></div><div class=\"doc-text-block\"><p><strong>Specific Camera</strong></p><p>Direct reference to a level camera</p></div><div class=\"doc-text-block\"><p><strong>Shake</strong></p><p>Camera shake class to play</p></div><div class=\"doc-text-block\"><p><strong>Blend In / Out Time</strong></p><p>Transition length</p></div><div class=\"doc-text-block\"><p><strong>Hide Player? / Hide NPC?</strong></p><p>Hide a character during the shot</p></div><div class=\"doc-text-block\"><p><strong>Propogate To Children?</strong></p><p>Hide attached child components too</p></div><div class=\"doc-text-block\"><p><strong>Ignore Player Camera Return On End?</strong></p><p>Skip the blend back to the player</p></div><h3 id=\"cameras-camera-shakes\">Camera Shakes</h3><p>In <code>Blueprints/CameraShakes</code>:</p><ul><li><code>BP_CS_Light</code>: subtle</li><li><code>BP_CS_Heavy</code>: strong impact</li><li><code>BP_CS_Rumble</code>: continuous</li></ul><p>Any <code>CameraShakeBase</code> child works</p><h3 id=\"cameras-component-level-settings\">Component-Level Settings</h3><div class=\"doc-text-block\"><p>Property</p><p>Description</p></div><div class=\"doc-text-block\"><p><strong>Use NPC Camera?</strong></p><p>Use the NPC's attached camera</p></div><div class=\"doc-text-block\"><p><strong>Camera Blend In Time</strong></p><p>Default blend into dialogue cameras</p></div><div class=\"doc-text-block\"><p><strong>Use Camera Blend Out? / 🎥 Camera Blend Out Time</strong></p><p>Blend back out on end</p></div><div class=\"doc-text-block\"><p><strong>🔴 Disable Camera Movement?</strong></p><p>Lock player camera input</p></div><div class=\"doc-text-block\"><p><strong>⚙ GASP Camera?</strong></p><p>Game Animation Sample compatibility</p></div><h3 id=\"cameras-tips\">Tips</h3><ul><li>Data Table imports can assign cameras by name</li><li>The Editor Utility previews each branch's camera</li><li><code>BP_MovingActor</code> works as a spline camera rail (see Moving Actor & Camera Tracker)</li></ul>"
  },
  {
   "id": "in-world",
   "num": "14",
   "icon": "💬",
   "title": "In World Dialogue",
   "lede": "Floating dialogue bubbles for ambient chatter and minor NPCs.",
   "html": "<h3 id=\"in-world-in-world-dialogue\">In World Dialogue</h3><p>Shows dialogue on a floating widget above the actor. No full-screen UI. Great for ambient chatter, signs, and minor NPCs</p><div class=\"doc-figure\"><img class=\"doc-img\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/docs/pie_inworld.jpg\" data-full=\"assets/docs/pie_inworld.jpg\" alt=\"\" style=\"max-width:700px\"></div><h3 id=\"in-world-setup\">Setup</h3><p>Your actor needs a <code>Dialogue_Component</code> first (see Getting Started)</p><div class=\"doc-step\"><div class=\"doc-step-text\"><p><strong>1.</strong> Click <strong>(+ Add)</strong> in Components</p><p><strong>2.</strong> Add <strong><code>BP_DC_InWorld</code></strong>, then select it</p></div><div class=\"doc-step-media\"><img class=\"doc-img\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/docs/iw_step1.png\" data-full=\"assets/docs/iw_step1.png\" alt=\"\" style=\"max-width:400px\"></div></div><div class=\"doc-step\"><div class=\"doc-step-text\"><p><strong>3.</strong> Check its Details:</p><p><strong>Widget Class</strong> = <code>W_Dialogue_InWorld</code> (default)</p><p><strong>Space</strong> = World (default)</p><p><strong>⚙ Settings</strong> sizes the bubble:</p><p><strong>Rotate to Player?</strong>: face the player</p><p><strong>Use Values Below?</strong>: apply the sizing values</p><p><strong>Widget / Text Scale</strong>, <strong>Size Width / Height</strong>, <strong>Text Padding</strong></p><p>Set <strong>Location</strong> above the head (example: Z = 130)</p></div><div class=\"doc-step-media\"><img class=\"doc-img\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/docs/iw_step2.png\" data-full=\"assets/docs/iw_step2.png\" alt=\"\" style=\"max-width:450px\"></div></div><div class=\"doc-step\"><div class=\"doc-step-text\"><p><strong>4.</strong> Select <strong>Dialogue_Component</strong>. Search <strong>\"inworld\"</strong></p><p>Set <strong>⚙ In World Widget?</strong> = <code>true</code></p></div><div class=\"doc-step-media\"><img class=\"doc-img\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/docs/iw_step3.png\" data-full=\"assets/docs/iw_step3.png\" alt=\"\" style=\"max-width:450px\"></div></div><div class=\"doc-text-block\"><p><strong>5.</strong> Author branches as normal. Rich text works too</p></div><h3 id=\"in-world-notes\">Notes</h3><ul><li>Pair with <strong>⚙ Auto Complete</strong> and <strong>Start On Overlap</strong> for ambient lines</li><li>The widget fades out when dialogue ends</li><li>All settings are editable per level instance too</li></ul><h3 id=\"in-world-examples\">Examples</h3><p><code>Examples/InWorld</code>: <code>BP_NPC_InWorld_01</code> and <code>BP_NPC_InWorld_02</code>. Duplicate one as a starting point</p>"
  },
  {
   "id": "events",
   "num": "15",
   "icon": "🔌",
   "title": "Events & Blueprint Nodes",
   "lede": "Dispatchers, runtime condition nodes, and helper functions for integrations.",
   "html": "<h3 id=\"events-events-blueprint-nodes\">Events & Blueprint Nodes</h3><p>Hook your own systems into the Dialogue Component</p><h3 id=\"events-event-dispatchers\">Event Dispatchers</h3><p>Bind from any blueprint (<strong>Bind Event to...</strong>):</p><div class=\"doc-text-block\"><p>Dispatcher</p><p>Fires when</p></div><div class=\"doc-text-block\"><p><strong>ED DC Begin Play</strong></p><p>Component initializes</p></div><div class=\"doc-text-block\"><p><strong>ED Dialogue Started</strong></p><p>Conversation begins</p></div><div class=\"doc-text-block\"><p><strong>ED Dialogue Continued</strong></p><p>Dialogue advances a branch</p></div><div class=\"doc-text-block\"><p><strong>ED Dialogue Ended</strong></p><p>Conversation ends</p></div><div class=\"doc-text-block\"><p><strong>ED Dialogue Ended / Continued</strong></p><p>Either of the above</p></div><div class=\"doc-text-block\"><p><strong>ED Fully Ended</strong></p><p>Fully closed, UI fade included</p></div><div class=\"doc-text-block\"><p><strong>ED Interact Button Pressed / Released</strong></p><p>Interact input pressed / released</p></div><div class=\"doc-text-block\"><p><strong>ED Input Received</strong></p><p>Any dialogue input</p></div><div class=\"doc-text-block\"><p><strong>ED Overlap / ED End Overlap</strong></p><p>Player enters / leaves range</p></div><div class=\"doc-text-block\"><p><strong>ED Camera Changed (Level Selected)</strong></p><p>Switched to a level camera</p></div><div class=\"doc-text-block\"><p><strong>ED Secondary Log</strong></p><p>Secondary log written</p></div><div class=\"doc-text-block\"><p><strong>ED Stop Audio</strong></p><p>Dialogue audio stopped</p></div><div class=\"doc-text-block\"><p><strong>ED Text Generation Ended</strong></p><p>Typewriter finished a line</p></div><div class=\"doc-text-block\"><p><strong>ED Widget Removed</strong></p><p>Dialogue widget removed</p></div><div class=\"doc-text-block\"><p><strong>ED Continue After Rotation</strong></p><p>Rotation finished, dialogue continues</p></div><p><code>BP_Scroll</code> also exposes <strong>ED Picked Up</strong></p><p>Use these for quests, achievements, cutscenes, AI, and saves</p><h3 id=\"events-starting-dialogue-from-blueprints\">Starting Dialogue From Blueprints</h3><div class=\"doc-text-block\"><p>Node</p><p>Use</p></div><div class=\"doc-text-block\"><p><strong>Start Dialogue Externally</strong></p><p>Start any actor's dialogue remotely</p></div><div class=\"doc-text-block\"><p><strong>Force Start Dialogue</strong></p><p>Start the owner's dialogue directly</p></div><div class=\"doc-text-block\"><p><strong>On Specific Branch</strong></p><p>Run logic when a branch is reached. Empty actor pin = owner</p></div><p>Dialogue creation macros and tree templates also exist. Build or update branches from blueprints, editor or runtime</p><h3 id=\"events-conditions-at-runtime\">Conditions At Runtime</h3><div class=\"doc-text-block\"><p>Node</p><p>What it does</p></div><div class=\"doc-text-block\"><p><strong>Change Player Condition Single</strong></p><p>Add or subtract one condition</p></div><div class=\"doc-text-block\"><p><strong>Set Player Condition Amount</strong></p><p>Hard-set one condition</p></div><div class=\"doc-text-block\"><p><strong>Change Player Conditions Multiple</strong></p><p>Add/subtract a map at once</p></div><div class=\"doc-text-block\"><p><strong>Set Player Conditions Multiple</strong></p><p>Hard-set a map at once</p></div><p>Single changes auto-save. A library check tests for any or N condition properties</p><h3 id=\"events-helper-library\">Helper Library</h3><p><code>BP_DC_Library</code>, callable anywhere:</p><div class=\"doc-text-block\"><p>Function</p><p>Use</p></div><div class=\"doc-text-block\"><p><strong>BPL Get Dialogue Component</strong></p><p>From any actor</p></div><div class=\"doc-text-block\"><p><strong>Get Player Character's Dialogue Component</strong></p><p>Player shortcut</p></div><div class=\"doc-text-block\"><p><strong>Get DC Player's Save REF</strong></p><p>The save object (see Save System)</p></div><p><strong>Get Currently Talking Actor</strong> (on the component) returns the current speaker</p>"
  },
  {
   "id": "scrolls",
   "num": "16",
   "icon": "📜",
   "title": "Scrolls, Pickups & Quests",
   "lede": "Pickups that grant conditions and change dialogue state.",
   "html": "<h3 id=\"scrolls-scrolls-pickups-quests\">Scrolls, Pickups & Quests</h3><p><code>BP_Scroll</code> is a pickup that changes dialogue state. NPCs react to items with zero blueprint logic</p><h3 id=\"scrolls-bp_scroll\">BP_Scroll</h3><p>On pickup, it can grant conditions and change start branches</p><div class=\"doc-text-block\"><p>Property</p><p>Description</p></div><div class=\"doc-text-block\"><p><strong>Actors To Effect / Actor To Effect</strong></p><p>Who the pickup affects</p></div><div class=\"doc-text-block\"><p><strong>START</strong></p><p>Their new starting branch</p></div><div class=\"doc-text-block\"><p><strong>Conditions & Keys</strong></p><p>Conditions granted to the player</p></div><div class=\"doc-text-block\"><p><strong>Condition Type</strong></p><p>Add, subtract, or overwrite</p></div><div class=\"doc-text-block\"><p><strong>Reset Talk Once?</strong></p><p>Re-enable a <strong>Talk Once?</strong> actor</p></div><div class=\"doc-text-block\"><p><strong>Enable Input?</strong></p><p>Re-enable interaction on the target</p></div><div class=\"doc-text-block\"><p><strong>🔊 Pickup</strong></p><p>Pickup sound</p></div><div class=\"doc-text-block\"><p><strong>ED Picked Up</strong></p><p>Dispatcher for custom reactions</p></div><div class=\"doc-text-block\"><p><strong>👾 Debug?</strong></p><p>Print debug info</p></div><p>Picked-up scrolls persist through the save system</p><h3 id=\"scrolls-example-flow\">Example Flow</h3><p>1. A guard gates a choice on <code>Permit</code> (see Conditions) 2. A <code>BP_Scroll</code> grants <code>Permit 1</code> and updates the quest giver's <strong>START</strong> 3. Both NPCs now react on the next talk</p><p>Examples: <code>Examples/Pickup</code> (<code>BP_Pickup</code>, <code>BP_Book</code>) and the demo levels</p><h3 id=\"scrolls-quest-notifications-w_dc_quest\">Quest Notifications (W_DC_Quest)</h3><p>A toast widget: icon + text, fades in and out</p><p><strong>Important:</strong> it's visual only. It grants nothing. To make dialogue react, also call <strong>Change Player Condition Single</strong> (or use a <code>BP_Scroll</code>)</p>"
  },
  {
   "id": "examples",
   "num": "17",
   "icon": "🧪",
   "title": "Demo & Example Content",
   "lede": "Every demo level and example folder, mapped.",
   "html": "<h3 id=\"examples-demo-example-content\">Demo & Example Content</h3><p>Working content to open, study, and duplicate</p><div class=\"doc-figure\"><img class=\"doc-img\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/docs/pie_basic_dialogue.jpg\" data-full=\"assets/docs/pie_basic_dialogue.jpg\" alt=\"\" style=\"max-width:700px\"></div><h3 id=\"examples-demo-dialoguecomponentdemo\">Demo (<code>DialogueComponent/Demo</code>)</h3><div class=\"doc-text-block\"><p>Folder</p><p>What's inside</p></div><div class=\"doc-text-block\"><p><strong>Explanation</strong></p><p>One NPC per feature. First/third person, cameras, auto complete, logs, locations</p></div><div class=\"doc-text-block\"><p><strong>Showcase</strong></p><p>Full level: doors, keys, elevator, overlaps, alt buttons, spline helicopter</p></div><div class=\"doc-text-block\"><p><strong>Demo</strong></p><p>Story NPCs: shop, quest, name change, locations, cameras, AI walkers</p></div><div class=\"doc-text-block\"><p><strong>BP_DC_TPC</strong></p><p>The demo player. Copy its nodes into your character (see Getting Started)</p></div><h3 id=\"examples-examples-dialoguecomponentexamples\">Examples (<code>DialogueComponent/Examples</code>)</h3><div class=\"doc-text-block\"><p>Folder</p><p>Demonstrates</p></div><div class=\"doc-text-block\"><p><strong>Horror</strong></p><p>Mood: post process + lighting + dialogue</p></div><div class=\"doc-text-block\"><p><strong>Interrogation</strong></p><p>Condition-gated, grayed-out choices</p></div><div class=\"doc-text-block\"><p><strong>InWorld</strong></p><p>Floating in-world dialogue widgets</p></div><div class=\"doc-text-block\"><p><strong>Multiple</strong></p><p>Data Table imports; dialogue alongside combat</p></div><div class=\"doc-text-block\"><p><strong>Patrol</strong></p><p>A patrolling, talkable NPC</p></div><div class=\"doc-text-block\"><p><strong>Pickup</strong></p><p>Items that change dialogue state</p></div><div class=\"doc-text-block\"><p><strong>Saving</strong></p><p>Save/load, cutscene, persistent destroyed actor</p></div><div class=\"doc-text-block\"><p><strong>Sidescroller</strong></p><p>2D/side-scroller camera setup</p></div><p>Fastest path: duplicate the closest example, edit its branches</p>"
  },
  {
   "id": "faq",
   "num": "02",
   "icon": "❓",
   "title": "FAQ & Troubleshooting",
   "lede": "Fixes for movement, interaction visuals, and hair groom issues.",
   "html": "<h3 id=\"faq-cant-move\">🚫 Can't Move?</h3><div class=\"doc-step\"><div class=\"doc-step-text\"><p>UE 5.1+ uses <b>Enhanced Input</b>, not the old Input Actions</p><p>METHOD 1</p><p>The demo character has a commented enhanced-inputs node group:</p></div><div class=\"doc-step-media\"><img class=\"doc-img\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/docs/d9bdcac7-0ade-445e-886d-c9ea499f9db6.png\" data-full=\"assets/docs/d9bdcac7-0ade-445e-886d-c9ea499f9db6.png\" alt=\"Enhanced Input Example\" style=\"max-width:700px\"></div></div><div class=\"doc-step\"><div class=\"doc-step-text\"><p>Copy/paste it anywhere in your Blueprint. Movement works:</p></div><div class=\"doc-step-media\"><img class=\"doc-img\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/docs/2add6f58-8392-4d31-8020-e2f945d98346.png\" data-full=\"assets/docs/2add6f58-8392-4d31-8020-e2f945d98346.png\" alt=\"Blueprint Placement Example\" style=\"max-width:700px\"></div></div><p><br><br>METHOD 2 <br><br>You can import the default inputs via <strong>Project Settings → Input</strong>, or download the preset config files:<br><br>🔗 <a href=\"https://mega.nz/file/JPkHFKqL#qfZGzDph4j6H_jMm832cXOBdoCDDdXjsV6HY7VJPi9s\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Download Default Inputs</a><br><br><p align=\"center\"></p><p align=\"center\"></p> |</p><div class=\"doc-figure\"><img class=\"doc-img\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/docs/a938dc34-9d0e-42d2-9188-60439f1cf880.png\" data-full=\"assets/docs/a938dc34-9d0e-42d2-9188-60439f1cf880.png\" alt=\"\"><img class=\"doc-img\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/docs/322d47ee-033a-4a0f-b003-de7fc8166f83.png\" data-full=\"assets/docs/322d47ee-033a-4a0f-b003-de7fc8166f83.png\" alt=\"\"></div><h3 id=\"faq-remove-outline-icon-interaction-ring\">🧼 Remove Outline, Icon, Interaction Ring</h3><div class=\"doc-step\"><div class=\"doc-step-text\"><p>Select the NPC's <strong>Dialogue Component</strong>. Set these bools to <code>false</code>:</p></div><div class=\"doc-step-media\"><img class=\"doc-img\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/docs/0e7df6e4-8287-49a3-a971-bcfc0000278c.png\" data-full=\"assets/docs/0e7df6e4-8287-49a3-a971-bcfc0000278c.png\" alt=\"\">\n<img class=\"doc-img\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/docs/8c24989a-d95b-4011-87d7-c652c2ee5179.png\" data-full=\"assets/docs/8c24989a-d95b-4011-87d7-c652c2ee5179.png\" alt=\"\">\n<img class=\"doc-img\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/docs/ce487df5-e861-45bf-bb5e-19775c5982e6.png\" data-full=\"assets/docs/ce487df5-e861-45bf-bb5e-19775c5982e6.png\" alt=\"\"></div></div><h3 id=\"faq-hair-groom-turns-red-afro\">💇 Hair Groom Turns Red / Afro?</h3><div class=\"doc-step\"><div class=\"doc-step-text\"><p>Groom turns red or deforms in dialogue?</p><p>✅ <strong>Fix:</strong> On the groom component, set <code>Override Settings = true</code> and <code>Enable Simulation = true</code></p></div><div class=\"doc-step-media\"><img class=\"doc-img\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/docs/8f677549-6122-4766-8217-d1798ac950a0.png\" data-full=\"assets/docs/8f677549-6122-4766-8217-d1798ac950a0.png\" alt=\"\">\n<img class=\"doc-img\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/docs/0d4b7596-b845-433b-9477-29dddbd5d4ee.png\" data-full=\"assets/docs/0d4b7596-b845-433b-9477-29dddbd5d4ee.png\" alt=\"\"></div></div>"
  },
  {
   "id": "changelog",
   "num": "01",
   "icon": "🗒️",
   "title": "Change Log",
   "lede": "Every update, newest first.",
   "html": "<h3 id=\"changelog-2132026\">2/13/2026</h3><ul><li>Added binding on actor destroyed, destroy interaction ring (when destroying actor outside of dialogue)</li></ul><h3 id=\"changelog-2102026\">2/10/2026</h3><ul><li>Added bools to save settings, allowing you to toggle whether or not load certain properties</li><li>Fixed Action example in the demo level (actor who opens the door) so that if using save, the door is raised even if you exited dialogue/game before it finished opening</li><li>Fixed \"Apply to all\" function: it would completely remove any dialogue audio you had for each branch</li></ul><h3 id=\"changelog-12142025\">12/14/2025</h3><ul><li>Added In World Dialogue widget display (for things like non-important dialogue/actors)</li><li>Added logic to start auto complete upon text display completing (before auto complete would begin immediately, even if text was still being typed. Would result in completing typed text, not progressing it. Doesn't effect instant text)</li><li>Fixed save game for picks (bp scroll would get destroyed but not save, now it does</li><li>Added save game logic to save actors using \"Talk Once\"</li></ul><h3 id=\"changelog-11252025\">11/25/2025</h3><ul><li>Removed unnecessary Debug variables (so struct directly influences)</li><li>Removed unnecessary Name variables (so struct directly influences)</li><li>Removed unnecessary Trace variables (so struct directly influences)</li><li>Added ability to assign camera by name on data table import</li><li>Added pass & fail conditions, that way you can easily adjust conditions</li><li>Improved Editor Utility interface</li><li>Improved Editor Utility speed</li><li>Fixed warning log about scrollbox</li><li>Fixed warning about spawning from empty class</li><li>Fixed tool tip to work even on disabled buttons (useful for letting player know why a choice is unable to be selected)</li><li>Fixed conditions bug on continue choices</li><li>Fixed icon widget visibility (it was blocking mouse input for alt buttons)</li><li>Fixed bug when going from overlapping auto start not destroying self if begin talking to another actor</li></ul><h3 id=\"changelog-9222025\">9/22/2025</h3><ul><li>Fixed interaction ring not reappearing upon dialogue ending</li><li>Added individual collapsible variable groups in editor utility</li><li>Added logic to stop montage when dialogue finishes (useful when animation was full body, because you'd move and legs would be stiff)</li></ul><h3 id=\"changelog-9112025\">9/11/2025</h3><ul><li>Added logic so that refreshing widget will automatically select dialogue component in your details panel</li><li>Test condition choices in preview widget</li></ul><h3 id=\"changelog-9102025\">9/10/2025</h3><ul><li>Added ability to interact with dialogue in editor preview</li><li>Added ability to scale UI & preview window with mouse & keyboard</li><li>Added Function Typer</li><li>Added keyboard shortcuts</li><li>Added arrow key & d-pad inputs</li><li>[Control + P] Toggle preview window</li><li>[Alt + R] Refreshes selected</li><li>[Arrow Left/Right] Previous/Next branch</li></ul><h3 id=\"changelog-912025\">9/1/2025</h3><ul><li>Added a comment of 5.1+ enhanced inputs to paste instead of needing to import default inputs</li><li>Updated \"On Specific Branch\" macro to allow for a pin to specify which actor's dialogue component to use (leaving empty works as is, checking owning actor's dialogue component</li><li>Added new BML that will check for any or specific # of condition properties</li><li>Fixed bug where non-choice button showed up as a choice after talking to a choice-based actor</li><li>Fixed crashing due to old editor utility</li></ul><h3 id=\"changelog-632025\">6/3/2025</h3><p>> [!TIP] > Updated Rich Text / Icons to work with any text length<br> > Added logic to hide/disable choices if player doesn't meet conditions<br></p><p>> [!CAUTION] > <code>UI</code> folder has been renamed to <code>Textures</code> <br></p><ul><li>Removed selected actor reference in editor utility, allowing you to delete without the reference window popping up</li><li>Added logic for button input running when released instead of pressed, and pressing and dragging off the button then releasing will negate input</li><li>Cleaned up editor utility logic so preview camera reflects current branch camera</li><li>Fixed accessed none error when importing data tables</li><li>Removed unnecessary variable filters in editor utility</li><li>Pinned top portion of editor utility</li><li>Fixed issue where ending dialogue outside the dialogue ring wasn't re-enabling interaction</li><li>Added widget preview to the editor utility</li><li>Fixed primary and secondary logs and added enum drop-down to select which to use</li><li>Fixed moving actor construct script warnings</li><li>Moved BP_MovingActor to main blueprints folder</li></ul><h3 id=\"changelog-412025\">4/1/2025</h3><ul><li>Added 'skip' button</li></ul><h3 id=\"changelog-3262025\">3/26/2025</h3><ul><li>Added <a href=\"https://github.com/dylogaming/Dialogue-Component/wiki/24.-Data-Tables\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Data Table</a> documentation</li><li>Code cleanup in Editor Utility</li></ul><h3 id=\"changelog-3102025\">3/10/2025</h3><ul><li>Cleaned up blueprint-created dialogue macros</li><li>Added \"Start Dialogue Externally\" node which allows you to trigger dialogues of any specified actor that has DC</li><li>Added enum on player choices to allow you to reset NPC rotation to original facing direction when choice is made (you'd typically use this on dialogue end)</li><li>Fixed continue button being flipped on default and flipping when hovering</li><li>Fixed continue button colors not being applied when adding a texture</li><li>Reverted BP_Combat blueprint to default settings (I had tweaked the blueprint when testing with it in the test level, modifying the one in the Dialogue_Blueprints level)</li></ul><h3 id=\"changelog-242025\">2/4/2025</h3><ul><li>Optimized textures, reducing overall asset size</li><li>Added macros to allow for dialogue creation & branch updating using blueprints in editor & runtime</li><li>Added pseudo-dialogue tree templates</li><li>Added bool to allow you to use UI struct or edit dialogue widget blueprint directly</li><li>Made it so rich text will type 1 character at a time (before it would auto-fill and only type default letters 1 at a time)</li><li>Fixed issue where if using \"Set actor location\" to true on multiple branches would sometimes put the player through the ground</li><li>Updated Player Location mesh to an arrow instead of a ball, allowing you to tell what direction the player will face</li></ul><h3 id=\"changelog-172025\">1/7/2025</h3><ul><li>Visibility tag array added, allowing you to specify which parts of an actor you want to adjust visibility</li></ul><h3 id=\"changelog-12262024\">12/26/2024</h3><ul><li>Added scrollbox to editor utility widget, allowing for better usability</li><li>Converted nameplate & sprite images back to object variables allowing for animated sprites</li><li>Added functionality for animated sprites</li></ul><h3 id=\"changelog-1292024\">12/9/2024</h3><ul><li>Added variable to play level sequences & set options under ➕ Extra Settings for both player & NPC</li></ul><div class=\"doc-figure\"><img class=\"doc-img\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/docs/b1e31413-3b79-441b-afa2-df8e30f60c9f.png\" data-full=\"assets/docs/b1e31413-3b79-441b-afa2-df8e30f60c9f.png\" alt=\"image\"></div><h3 id=\"changelog-10242024\">10/24/2024</h3><ul><li>Fixed bug where \"start on overlap\" dialogues that ended on the same branch would result in looping the convo</li><li>Fixed Nameplate & Sprite NPCs from causing issues with UI</li><li>Fixed bug where \"Hide UI this branch\" being true would flash on ending dialogue</li><li>Cleared default \"Name Search\" replacement from default being \"Player\" because it would constantly get changed in default example dialogues</li><li>Updated object references to soft references in BP_MovingActor (increases efficiency & allows you to save instance selected to blueprint w/o issue)</li><li>Fixed Showcase level \"ally\" dialogue not updating after opening the gate</li><li>Fixed bug where overlapping another actor while current dialogue plays wasn't ending current one and starting overlapped one</li><li>Alt button choices now use the UI Preset (still going to work on this more)</li><li>Alt buttons can be clicked on with mouse</li></ul><h3 id=\"changelog-10222024\">10/22/2024</h3><ul><li>Added validation to mesh variables allowing for 2D paper characters to work</li><li>Removed \"look at player\" bool from camera struct since it's no longer being used</li><li>Added tool tips to camera struct properties</li><li>Cleaned up Wraith in demo area</li><li>Fixed bug where attached cine cameras (not preset ones) wouldn't be used</li><li>Added scroll box style variable so you can easily hide edge shadows</li><li>Changed \"Fade In/Out\" to Fade & updated code to forward/reverse</li><li>Added fade out of dialogue UI</li><li>Removed Event Tick from Dialogue Widget (Wasn't even being used 🤦🏻‍♂️)</li></ul><h3 id=\"changelog-9192024\">9/19/2024</h3><ul><li>Added ability to import data tables which can format into branches</li></ul><div class=\"doc-figure\"><img class=\"doc-img\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/docs/c9d237e8-e1c1-4849-b353-dbb586e995eb.gif\" data-full=\"assets/docs/c9d237e8-e1c1-4849-b353-dbb586e995eb.gif\" alt=\"GIF 9-19-2024 5-45-43 PM\"></div><div class=\"doc-figure\"><img class=\"doc-img\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/docs/c99d1c68-20dc-4efd-8116-34b9408b4192.png\" data-full=\"assets/docs/c99d1c68-20dc-4efd-8116-34b9408b4192.png\" alt=\"image\"></div><p>Player options now allow for:</p><ul><li>Disabling interaction with NPCs which will also hide the outline & icon</li></ul><ul><li>Overwriting conditions, allowing you to perform a hard set on the values instead of only adding/subtracting</li></ul><div class=\"doc-figure\"><img class=\"doc-img\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/docs/727a6a77-611b-43f9-b461-d62659b61e59.png\" data-full=\"assets/docs/727a6a77-611b-43f9-b461-d62659b61e59.png\" alt=\"image\"></div><h3 id=\"changelog-962024\">9/6/2024</h3><ul><li>Updated Editor Utility</li></ul><p>Now all the variables are visible for branches and player choices</p><div class=\"doc-figure\"><img class=\"doc-img\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/docs/4f259800-e715-4137-bb04-8962f9aa4784.gif\" data-full=\"assets/docs/4f259800-e715-4137-bb04-8962f9aa4784.gif\" alt=\"\" style=\"max-width:50px\"></div><ul><li>Added inputs for changing player choice selection</li></ul><div class=\"doc-figure\"><img class=\"doc-img\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/docs/2f683bcf-8596-4cde-88f2-2016ec7f9981.png\" data-full=\"assets/docs/2f683bcf-8596-4cde-88f2-2016ec7f9981.png\" alt=\"image\"></div><h3 id=\"changelog-882024\">8/8/2024</h3><ul><li>Fixed montage bug where player montage would play on NPC</li></ul><h3 id=\"changelog-6252024\">6/25/2024</h3><ul><li>Added Dialogue Editor Utility widget</li><li>Updated camera & activator variables to soft actor references, now allowing you to save referenced actors</li><li>Updated dialogue system from maps to arrays</li></ul><h3 id=\"changelog-3202024\">3/20/2024</h3><ul><li>Fixed explanation level dialogue that had clashing name replacement</li><li>Fixed explanation level auto-complete example would generate text block if player spammed input</li><li>Began working on new example NPC blueprint using 2 new camera components</li><li>Fixed alt buttons were not showing (made separate alt button widget) due to choice buttons clashing</li></ul><h3 id=\"changelog-292024\">2/9/2024</h3><ul><li>Added actor outline which highlights actor to talk to, when in range</li><li>Added dynamic name replacement – system will auto-populate names for speakers and when names are detected in dialogues</li><li>Added option to switch focused sprites during dialogues – darkens whoever isn’t talking</li><li>Updated editor functions & added nameplate & sprite function</li><li>Fixed sprite not showing unless using nameplate</li><li>Added “DC Owner” variable to replace ‘Get Owner” node</li><li>Fixed setting mesh variable so that any mesh, not just skeletal meshes will be detected</li><li>Fixed color for sprite tints (variable existed in struct but was not plugged into anything)</li><li>Added icon background as a variable in Icon struct</li><li>Added logic so if no icon background is placed, it will be transparent and still show the icon</li></ul><h3 id=\"changelog-v-22\">V 2.2</h3><ul><li>Added Changelog to track updates</li><li>Organized functions, macros, and variables</li><li>Added NPC location which moves NPC characters to selected location during dialogue, and will change dialogue when location is reached</li><li>Added validation to blueprint library functions resolving errors when simulating</li><li>Removed Paragon & Trooper materials & textures to reduce file size</li><li>Consolidated icon fade animation to 1 forward/reverse</li><li>Added bool for Location / 2D dialogue audio</li></ul>"
  }
 ]
};
